WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:01.960
[contemplative music]

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:03.336
What would it take

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.505
to build a more perfect world?

00:00:06.464 --> 00:00:09.259
With nations at peace.

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:11.511
A healthier planet
for our children.

00:00:12.595 --> 00:00:15.765
And prosperity for all.

00:00:16.808 --> 00:00:19.227
What knowledge will we need?

00:00:19.227 --> 00:00:21.855
What values will unite us?

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:24.149
Who will lead the way?

00:00:24.149 --> 00:00:27.152
Today, humanity
is faced with challenges

00:00:27.152 --> 00:00:30.405
that are growing increasingly
serious and complex.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:34.784
Climate change
and environmental degradation.

00:00:35.493 --> 00:00:37.871
Political extremism and war.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.040
Economic development
and disparity.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.669
Migration and global health.

00:00:46.254 --> 00:00:49.048
The hope of a prosperous future
will require

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:51.676
commitment, passion
and planning.

00:00:52.135 --> 00:00:55.013
A multidisciplinary approach
to problem solving.

00:00:55.638 --> 00:00:58.349
A willingness
to consider diverse viewpoints.

00:00:58.808 --> 00:01:02.145
And an abiding belief
in our ability to find answers

00:01:02.145 --> 00:01:03.062
together.

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:06.024
With wisdom, facts, insight

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:07.984
and courage.

00:01:09.694 --> 00:01:13.323
For more than 300 years,
Yale has advanced humanity's

00:01:13.323 --> 00:01:15.742
understanding of complex
global issues

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:19.078
and educated leaders
committed to addressing them.

00:01:20.163 --> 00:01:21.247
By establishing the

00:01:21.247 --> 00:01:23.958
Yale Jackson
School of Global Affairs,

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.544
we further
underscore our commitment

00:01:26.544 --> 00:01:28.838
to cultivate
an intimate community

00:01:28.838 --> 00:01:32.759
of outstanding faculty,
seasoned practitioners

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:36.387
and students who will study
and develop policy

00:01:36.387 --> 00:01:38.681
to address
the challenges of today

00:01:38.973 --> 00:01:41.434
and the opportunities
of tomorrow.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:44.521
To advance Yale's mission
with outstanding research

00:01:44.521 --> 00:01:47.357
and scholarship, education
and practice.

00:01:48.358 --> 00:01:50.443
To prepare students
for leadership

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.613
and service on the global stage.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.448
To be a champion for light

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:58.284
and truth in the world.

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:01.830
To all of you who have helped
make the Yale Jackson

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:05.124
School of Global Affairs
possible— thank you.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:09.087
And to those who will lead
on behalf of humanity,

00:02:10.088 --> 00:02:12.340
the future belongs to you.

